jobs.description:
**Role Overview**

You will be a core technical force ensuring the stable operation of the company's critical infrastructure, keeping computing facilities ready for 24/7 operation. You will also serve as the primary technical liaison during official site visits and third\-party audits, professionally addressing infrastructure\-related questions.

**Key Responsibilities**

* Lead site selection and on\-site surveys for data center facilities; deliver professional survey reports and drive business coordination to ensure smooth facility deployment;
* Coordinate with system integrators on networking solutions, and follow through on procurement progress and implementation;
* Lead technical inspections and provide professional guided tours and technical Q\&A for visiting auditors, inspection agencies, and business partners;
* Maintain accurate and complete operations logs, incident reports, and equipment asset inventories.

**Requirements**

* 2\+ years of hands\-on experience in data center or critical facility operations and maintenance;
* Excellent verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain technical information clearly and confidently to non\-technical audiences;
* Ability to work independently and under pressure, with rigorous and meticulous documentation habits;
* Flexibility to accommodate occasional on\-site presence in California.

Pay: $95,000\.00 \- $135,000\.00 per year

Benefits:

* 401(k)
* Relocation assistance

Work Location: Hybrid remote in San Francisco, CA 94104

